From 9fa5abe69e0e25487cba5e16892ac9ed37186df0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Basin Battle <basin@battle>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 12:01:34 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Westbrook Garrison is gone: the barracks and its clutter
 hidden, the ground under it filled

A small table of world edits (benilla-formats `world_edits`, map 0 only; it mirrors htl-map's
WESTBROOK_EDITS, which the Elwynn Survival server builds its land from, and must change with it)
is applied where an ADT tile is parsed into chunks and placements, so the terrain mesh, its
collider, the ground clutter, every height query and the WMO and doodad streams agree: the
barracks WMO (MODF 71670) and the twelve barrels, crates, jars and bucket round it (MDDF 71666-71669,
17030-17037) are not there (not drawn, no collision, no interior light), and every chunk touching
the 45 yd circle round (-9620, 690) has its terrain holes cleared, its own heights drawn and
walked. The streamed tile (AdtLoader) takes its map from its path; load_tile_mesh from its map.
